        <mxCell id="c219" value="Growth 40% Sensitivity" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#D5D8DC;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="188" y="721" width="196" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c220" value="&lt;i&gt;The model of Requirement 7&#x27;s growth test at 40%: minimize the total added cost, B21, by changing the units bought, L14:L19, with the hours used after buying (E6:E10) not above the practical capacity (B6:B10) and the units bought not above the units at growth (C14:C19). Finishing and Test binds: its slack is 0 and an hour of its capacity is worth 6.01 (column I, hidden). The values in L14:L19 are the optimum computed by the simplex method and written when the workbook was built; Solver itself was not run. The formula bar shows the hours used after buying at the first work center. Columns H to K and N to R are hidden here: the shadow price, the hours per unit at each work center and the plan the supplier would accept.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="751" width="860" height="83" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
